40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 3.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 14.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 8.0 to 26.2. Contract [1], for 39,750.23 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["D%2BOmlcbFp7h9PLkba5eRog%3D%3D","KA3qcVA%2FONsaF6cS8TCh%2FA%3D%3D","m%2FF6baOGNGacCF8sV%2BqtYA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}